e nasal cavity include:\n[RAG context for 'Initially' (score=0.63):]\n  Source: InternalMed_Harrison\n  Noninvasive Syndromes The two major noninvasive syndromes caused by S. pneumoniae are sinusitis and otitis media; the latter is the most common pneumococcal syndrome and most often affects young child\n[Indirect reasoning chains (clinical inference):]\n  worsening symptoms of previously diagnosed acute sinusitis despite decongestant use → treatment-resistant acute sinusitis due to anterior nasal foreign body → Anterior Nasal Foreign Body with Infection\n    (frequency: frequent)\n    Suggestion: Evaluate for unilateral foul-smelling purulent nasal discharge and perform anterior rhinoscopy to identify potential foreign body\n  persistent nasal symptoms with treatment failure → structural nasal obstruction complicating sinusitis → Vascular or Structural Nasal Abnormality\n    (frequency: occasional)\n    Suggestion: Assess for anatomical nasal obstruction (e.g., polyps, septal deviation) that could explain lack of response to decongestants\n\nWhen indirect_reasoning_chains are present, generate candidates that investigate the INTERMEDIATE phenotype to confirm or rule out the indirect association."}
